Subject: Cantor Self Work Lifecycle Admission P0 Solution

@ [solution_uuid] be2d0b14-2d7a-4aef-8f5a-83ff87fcd990
@ [canonical_uuid] 0ba80ace-d2ae-4846-b3fd-f954f28f84a5

& [Implementation]
  + one pure cantor_core module revalidates the complete SWA-02 proposal before constructing or advancing a lifecycle
  + every exact plan step receives one attempt identity and one distinct pending ready active stopped resumable failed awaiting-review or complete state
  + checkpoints bind the exact request sequence predecessor state map transition ledger evidence unresolved account and digest
  + legal transitions replay from BEGIN and dependency-ready successors are released only after exact predecessor completion

& [Security]
  + one active step is the maximum and failed attempts are terminal
  + start resume and completion retain opaque externally supplied receipt references but SWA-03 neither authenticates nor issues them
  + all eight work capabilities remain not_granted_pending_contract and representation_only prevents lifecycle state from becoming work authority
  + unknown fields work-plan drift dependency bypass state substitution illegal edges receipt absence causal mismatch and digest mutation fail closed

& [ProductPosition]
  + SWA-03 supplies the deterministic checkpoint and reentry substrate for an SOP-driven agent loop without performing the work
  + SWA-04 must separately broker proposed workspace updates physical mutation verification acceptance and rollback
